  "task": "X43 h=4 centered shell-size closure",
  "theorem": "Let m_s be nonzero pair-sum shell sizes.  X42 gives R_centered <= sum_s C(m_s,4).  If max_s m_s <=3 then every term vanishes.  If max_s m_s <=4, then C(m_s,4) is 1 only at m_s=4, so C(m_s,4) <= m_s/4 and R_centered <= (sum_s m_s)/4 < n^2.  Thus the centered affine branch is safely below the rewired n^3 terminal column under this one-number shell-size condition."
